reas due to gallstones.", "HORMONAL STUDIES:Tests conducted to evaluate adrenal function and assess the presence of conditions like Cushing's syndrome or hyperaldosteronism in patients with incidentalomas.", "HYPERALDOSTERONISM PRIMARIO:A condition that may be screened for in patients with adrenal incidentalomas, characterized by excessive production of aldosterone.", "HYPERALDOSTERONISMO PRIMARIO:A condition characterized by excessive production of aldosterone, often evaluated in patients with adrenal incidentalomas.", "DIURÉTICOS:Diuréticos, or diuretics, are medications that promote the excretion of water and salts from the body through urine. They are commonly used in the treatment of conditions such as hypertension and edema, as they help to alleviate fluid retention. Diuretics can significantly affect sodium levels and are relevant in the context of diagnosing conditions like SIADH (Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion). Additionally, they may influence the evaluation of adrenal function in patients with adrenal incidentalomas and can impact electrolyte balance, particularly in individuals with adrenal insufficiency.\n\nThese medications can also affect magnesium reabsorption in the kidneys, potentially leading to changes in magnesium levels and causing conditions such as hypomagnesemia or hypermagnesiuria. Furthermore, diuretics are known to promote the loss of potassium, which is an important consideration in their use. Overall, diuréticos play a crucial role in managing fluid balance and electrolyte levels in various medical conditions.", "ANTAGONISTAS DE LA ALDOSTERONA:A class of medications that block the effects of aldosterone, relevant in the context of hyperaldosteronism and adrenal incidentalomas.", "HORMONAS ADRENALINA:Hormones produced by the adrenal glands that are involved in the body's stress response, relevant in the context of adrenal tumors.", "ADENOMA BENIGNO:A benign tumor of the adrenal gland that rarely secretes sex hormones.", "HIDROXIPROGESTERONA:17-hidroxiprogesterona is a hormone that should be measured in cases of bilateral adrenal incidentalomas to rule out congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency.", "SUPRARRENAL:The term \"suprarrenal\" refers to the adrenal glands, which are located above the kidneys. These glands play a crucial role in the endocrine system, producing important hormones such as cortisol and adrenaline. In the context of medical conditions, suprarrenal glands are often discussed in relation to incidentalomas and disorders associated with them. Additionally, they are known to be the site where tumors such as feochromocitomas and paragangliomas can develop. Overall, the suprarrenal glands are vital components of the body's hormonal regulation and are involved in various health conditions.", "FAASSNACHT M:Fassnacht M is an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on the management of adrenal incidentalomas.", "ADRENOCORTICAL CARCINOMA:Adrenocortical carcinoma is a rare cancer of the adrenal cortex, with an incidence of 1 in 1,000,000 people per year, often requiring surgical intervention for localized disease.", "STEWARD PM:Steward PM is an author referenced in the literature regarding the adrenal cortex and its disorders.", "HIPOGONADISMO:Hipogonadismo es una condición médica caracterizada por concentraciones bajas de testosterona en sangre y un deterioro de la espermatogénesis. Esta condición se manifiesta cuando el cuerpo no produce suficientes hormonas sexuales, lo que puede dar lugar a diversos problemas de salud, incluyendo la infertilidad. Además, el hipogonadismo se asocia a menudo con una secreción reducida o ausente de hormonas desde las gónadas. En algunos casos, el tratamiento con mitotano puede estar relacionado con esta condición. En resumen, el hipogonadismo implica una deficiencia en la producción de testosterona y puede tener múltiples repercusiones en la salud general del individuo.", "CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL PRIMARIO:Carcinoma suprarrenal primario is a rare cancer with an incidence of 1 in 1,000,000 inhabitants per year, more frequently affecting women than men."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}